       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ordered:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. That is typically 800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual single-dose maximum.\n- **Risks:** This dose carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It also adds toxicity without added benefit, because analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n1. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum.\n2. **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, a typical analgesic dose.\n3. **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n4. **The dose is intended as written.** If so, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
