       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of serious harm to the patient. There's no dosing scenario I know of that makes it appropriate, and the order system wouldn't be a safeguard here.\n\nIf the goal is to have the plan settled this afternoon, I can enter one of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day). Your number may have been meant as a daily total.\n\nIf the patient's pain or inflammation needs more than this, you could add a scheduled acetaminophen order or choose a different agent. I can enter those too.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical indication that requires a dose above the labeled maximum, please discuss it with pharmacy. If they approve, the order can go through whatever override process your institution uses.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
